     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, and I can't enter it as written. I can't verify the specialist recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also twice the labeled maximum, and metformin has no added glucose-lowering effect above about 2,000-2,550 mg/day. Going higher mainly adds risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. If standard dosing failed, the usual next step is adding or switching to another agent, not raising metformin.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max) now. You can then discuss anything further with the specialist.\n- **If the specialist really wants 5,100 mg/day**, this should go through pharmacy verification or the specialist's own order, with the rationale documented. I'd suggest that route over my entering it.\n- **If the intended dose was different**, such as a transcription error, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 850 mg three times daily order?"
      }
     ],
